# local-02-qsa-fp8-kv, vLLM 0.31.0 version (budi, 2026-10-12): FP8-e4m3 main
# K/V for QSA on sm_86, on top of upstream #55557.
#
# 0.31.0 ships FP8 K/V for QSA (#55557): the backend accepts fp8, the cache is
# uint8, forward_qsa views it as float8_e4m3fn and the split-K kernel converts
# it with `.to()`. That conversion needs Triton's fp8e4nv type, which exists
# only on sm_89+: on a 3090 (and the 3060) the kernel fails to compile
# (checked 2026-10-12, Triton 3.7.1). Upstream also has no FP8 in the staged
# prefill and row-cache kernels, which come from the flash-next patches.
#
# What this patch does (only with --kv-cache-dtype fp8; BF16 is unchanged):
#   * Every QSA kernel (split-K, staged prefill, row cache) reads the cache as
#     uint8 and dequantizes through a 256-entry E4M3 -> BF16 table (exact).
#     Both dots then run in BF16 (this absorbs the 0.30 build's local-05:
#     no FP16 converts per tile; prefill kernels ~40% faster on sm_86).
#   * Scales follow upstream: host floats (layer._k_scale_float/_v_scale_float),
#     k folded into softmax_scale, v into the output normalizer. The staged and
#     row-cache kernels take the same runtime softmax_scale/output_scale.
#   * QSA host-KV offload: pinned pool and GPU slot use the cache dtype, so the
#     pool halves (2048 -> 1024 B/token/layer), and
#     _qsa_offload_bytes_per_token_per_layer counts the 1-byte slot.
#   * The table is created in bind_kv_cache, outside CUDA graph capture.
# Not needed any more (upstream has it): the backend dtype list,
# supports_kv_cache_dtype, and building FlashAttentionImpl with "auto".

